{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228141-a-louis-covenant","id":1228141,"title":"A Louis Covenant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-17T16:18:37-07:00","id":1228141,"title":"A Louis Covenant?","content":"For those unfamiliar, Louis is a character of the novel/film &quot;Interview with a Vampire&quot; who became a vampire, but was generally a good person. Naturally, the poor dude was tortured trying to reconcile his morals with his vampiric nature.<br /> <br /> So what about a Covenant of these kind of vampires? It'd be an uphill battle to be sure, considering the other Covenants. Still, I think there'd be enough Louis-types out there determined enough to establish one.<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm not the most familiar with Requiem, so I'm probably missing something here. Any resources out there for these types of vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T17:42:25-07:00","id":1228158,"title":"","content":"Generally if I've learned anything, it couldn't be a Covenant because merely joining a Covenant is a breaking point on the humanity scale. Covenants are in general used to help ease the minds of vampires as they descend into being a monster.<br /> <br /> Now, I could see a group of Kindred who loosely associate themselves together in trying to maintain their humanity, but I would believe they would remain apolitical and not truly gather themselves into a Covenant to prevent themselves from slipping down that slippery slope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T18:11:10-07:00","id":1228167,"title":"","content":"The Vampire Chronicles characters are kind of hard to translate because there are some significant differences between the settings (namely Anne Rice's stories assume a much smaller population of vampires). It's also difficult because the Vampire Chronicles are largely written from the point of view of characters, with different books contradicting each other based on differences of opinion, experience, and certain character bending the truth and even lying for personal reasons.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;can't be a Covenant&quot; because joining a Covenant is a breaking point isn't a good way of thinking about it. Any longer association of vampires is a breaking point on some level, because you're reminding yourself you're a vampire by hanging out with other vampires. It's a challenge that needs to be faced regardless of the level of organization.<br /> <br /> To an extent most of the existing Covenants have some appeal to the Louis types depending on their cultural background. The Carthians are probably the ones that best reflect Louis' particular arc, in the form of the more intellectual side of the Covenant. Louis isn't a bomb-throwing revolutionary, but he's constantly in search of a better way of doing things than the traditional vampires, and looks towards humans as inspiration for how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T22:25:54-07:00","id":1228205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228141-a-louis-covenant?p=1228167#post1228167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think &quot;can't be a Covenant&quot; because joining a Covenant is a breaking point isn't a good way of thinking about it. Any longer association of vampires is a breaking point on some level, because you're reminding yourself you're a vampire by hanging out with other vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even joining a covenant with the express purpose of maintaining Humanity might be a breaking point because it's an internal admission that that is something you can no longer do on your own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Carthians are probably the ones that best reflect Louis' particular arc, in the form of the more intellectual side of the Covenant. Louis isn't a bomb-throwing revolutionary, but he's constantly in search of a better way of doing things than the traditional vampires, and looks towards humans as inspiration for how. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. He also thought there were many types of good, which sounds more Carthian than any of the others.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T23:11:54-07:00","id":1228213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228141-a-louis-covenant?p=1228205#post1228205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even joining a covenant with the express purpose of maintaining Humanity might be a breaking point because it's an internal admission that that is something you can no longer do on your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it is a Breaking Point, you start the game at 7 because you're believed to have already joined a covenant, and being 'good' doesn't mean maintaining 10 Humanity, being independent, and never facing Breaking Points. They're a fact of (un)life, and the vampires that don't have ways to deal with them are the ones that spiral downward into draugr-dom. Covenants are basically a group-wide touchstone in the long-term. They may not keep you from facing Breaking Points, but they'll give you reasons not to become a draugr, and they all have workarounds to dealing with common vampire problems.<br /> <br /> There's some extra covenants in Danse Macabre, like the Sun-Walking Knights that might appeal to Louis, though he didn't seem to care much about people. But being good person who feels bad about what other vampires do (and you do too sometimes) is something that can play in every covenant. That described three of the games original signature characters, Persephone, Loki and Bruise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-18-2018, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T08:07:27-07:00","id":1228301,"title":"","content":"A Covenant isn't necessary; you could have a smaller association, or even a secret society. Here is something that might interest you (it uses 1st ed system, so update as desired):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Shadow Cult: The Path of the Man Ascendant </b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The war between Man and Beast rages within each vampire. More often than not, the Beast wins, or at least gains enough ground that the Man is barely recognizable from his breathing days. Yet there are many who stubbornly cling to what made them human \u2013 whether beliefs, interests, or friends. A few have chosen the narrow path back towards salvation, to become more human than most humans \u2013 to quiet the Beast as much as the animate dead can. They have chosen the Path of the Man Ascendant. </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">History: </span></b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The gentleman-philosopher Nathaniel Etheridge was Embraced as a Mekhet in 1718. In his first few decades he experienced the predictable loss of his morality to the Beast within. In 1761 Etheridge wrote that he was at the last turning point; he could accept the evil he had become and lose himself to the Beast, or he could claw his way back to the higher path, becoming the Man which even mortals aspire to. He saw the curse as lethal to what made one human, and decided to take the hard route. Over the next century, Etheridge intensively studied philosophy from around the world, watched the interactions of Kindred, and developed mental exercises to focus the will and clear the distractions and temptations of the Beast from the true path. In time, he found others who wished to rein in their inner monster, and taught them as best he could. The teacher dropped out of sight shortly after producing a few copies of his seminal work, <i>Testament of a Humanist</i>. As copies of the book circulated, a cult grew up around the philosopher\u2019s work, and continues to quietly expand.<br /> <br /> All this can be confirmed if one looks hard enough. The fate of Nathaniel Etheridge is unclear and controversial. The anonymous author of <i>The Lives and Deaths of a Humanist</i> claims that Etheridge reached Golconda, and chose to become mortal again. Humanists say the <i>Testament</i> is the more important work, and the claims of <i>Lives and Deaths</i>, even if true, are beside the point. Yet often these naysayers secretly hold the promise of Golconda deep in their hearts. </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Texts:</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Testament of a Humanist</i>. First published by Nathaniel Etheridge in 1924. The first section of the volume is largely autobiographical. The second section examines the nature of the beast and the effects of moral degeneration, drawing examples from various real-world Kindred to illustrate the points. The third section discusses beliefs, behaviors and exercises to refine the mind and retain and strengthen moral character. A final few pages discuss Golconda as myth and legend, and as a worthy goal (It does not claim factuality in this matter).<br /> <br /> <i>The Lives and Deaths of a Humanist</i> Copies first appeared in the 1990s. Written anonymously, it reiterates and elaborates on the biographical information in the <i>Testament</i>, and goes on to fill in the story of Etheridges\u2019 existence after 1923. It claims that Etheridge left his handful of disciples in 1943, questing for Golconda. According to the book, he reappeared to the author in the 1960s as a mortal, proclaiming that Golconda was a real transcendence. They continued to meet every few years until Etheridge died in 1990.<br /> <br /> <b>Praxis:</b> Cultist believe that they are cursed, pure and simple. Like an illness, the curse must be diligently treated, less it get worse and ultimately destroy the host. Humanists seek to strengthen the Man within, to cling to the vestiges of the human soul in their animate corpses. Members study and meditate. They stay close to mortals, developing connections that keep them engaged with the living world beyond the predator/prey mode. It is a dangerous practice \u2013 a moment\u2019s slip or bad luck could undo years of self-control, not to mention expose the vampire to unfriendly eyes. Also, should the cultist\u2019s beliefs and practices become known to other undead, the established Kindred hierarchy is liable to see a potential threat to the Masquerade \u2013 or use the Humanist\u2019s mortal ties against them.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Organization:</span></b> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Humanists often collect in small congregations, usually centered around a charismatic leader. Whether in a group or walking the path alone, most initiates try to distance themselves from Kindred society \u2013 both to avoid persecution and to reduce exposure to the immoral behaviors and temptations inherent in the vampire lifestyle. Yet, like most Kindred, they seldom stray from where mortals congregate, for without humanity to guide them, vampires would lose their way as easily as if they were in a depraved Prince\u2019s court.</span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Initiations</b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 The Humanists rely on mental discipline to focus the mind on what is right. The character gains the Merit: Meditative Mind.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 The Humanist gains an extra die to resist degeneration. This is for Humanity loss only, not for acquiring a derangement.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The Humanist\u2019s moral compass guides him to salvation. Once per chapter, the Storyteller may make an Intelligence + Composure roll. Success on this roll may be used to alert a player to the Humanity risks in a given course of action, and to suggest an alternative which poses less peril of Degeneration. Alternatively, the character may have a mental breakthrough on the path to regaining the soul \u2013 in other words, success shows the way to gain a dot of Humanity. Note that only one of these options is available for any one roll. The player may ask the Storyteller for a roll, but there is no obligation to comply.</span></td> </tr> </table></div> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Covenants: </span></b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The typical Humanist belongs to no covenant. Of those who do, the Carthian Movement is both more accepting and (sometimes) more palatable to those trying to keep their Humanity. Some members reside within the structure of the Invictus, although they do well to keep their initiation secret. The Ordo Dracul, while not actively persecuting the cult, feel that seeking to return to humanity rather than working to transcend vampirism is a backwards step at best. Members of the Lancea Sanctum feel that rejecting their divine role by seeking to become more human is heretical. The Circle of the Crone is even less tolerant, finding the Humanist view antithetical to their own beliefs.<br /> <br /> <b>Key words:</b> When talking with some suspected of also walking the Path, somewhere in an initial conversation a Humanist inserts, \u201cI lived many years ago.\u201d To which another Humanist would reply, \u201cAnd may you live again one day.\u201d</span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T10:01:36-07:00","id":1228319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228141-a-louis-covenant?p=1228301#post1228301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Covenant isn't necessary; you could have a smaller association, or even a secret society.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're talking about is a covenant. While the five 'main' ones are big, a covenant is just 'a faction of Kindred who share certain political or theological beliefs,' and can be as small as a coterie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T12:06:29-07:00","id":1228350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228141-a-louis-covenant?p=1228319#post1228319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you're talking about is a covenant. While the five 'main' ones are big, a covenant is just 'a faction of Kindred who share certain political or theological beliefs,' and can be as small as a coterie.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can look at them that way, sure. And I've had some pretty small groups that get called Covenants. But in general I don't use covenant that broadly. For example, I really don't see the Harbingers as a covenant -- they have something they agree on and a discipline growing out of it, but the concept is too thin to build a covenant (I did fold them in with a couple of other concepts and called it a covenant, however). Same with Children of the Thorns -- a wicked cool idea, but it lacks a depth and structure that says covenant to me. <br /> <br /> It's a matter of semantics, perhaps. <br /> <br /> If some Louis-types congregated to deal with their existential angst, it might be the vampire equivalent of the werewolf lodges. Call it what you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T12:28:18-07:00","id":1228353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228141-a-louis-covenant?p=1228350#post1228350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can look at them that way, sure. And I've had some pretty small groups that get called Covenants. But in general I don't use covenant that broadly....<br /> <br /> It's a matter of semantics, perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the definition from the Lexicon in the core book of both editions. If you don't want to call them covenants, call them whatever you want, but it's what they are. Some covenants (noted in Thousand Years of Night) stay secret because they want to, like the Body of a Nation, which originally just had five members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-18-2018, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T18:25:55-07:00","id":1228438,"title":"","content":"I don't wanna be that guy but... it's 'Interview With <b>The</b> Vampire'.<br /> <br /> Why do people always get the title wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T20:05:30-07:00","id":1228481,"title":"","content":"It's a simple mistake (especially for speakers of languages that handle articles differently).<br /> <br /> It's also a title that doesn't make perfect sense because the the story is largely from Louis' perspective, who is by far not &quot;the&quot; vampire, he's just &quot;a&quot; vampire. He's only &quot;the&quot; vampire to Daniel (who's not even named in Interview).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T00:08:40-07:00","id":1228513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228141-a-louis-covenant?p=1228438#post1228438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't wanna be that guy but... it's 'Interview With <b>The</b> Vampire'.<br /> <br /> Why do people always get the title wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they\u2019re thinking of Kingdom of Loathing:<br /> <a href=\"http://kol.coldfront.net/thekolwiki/index.php/Interview_With_You_(a_Vampire\" target=\"_blank\">http://kol.coldfront.net/thekolwiki/...You_(a_Vampire</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T06:12:37-07:00","id":1228556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228141-a-louis-covenant?p=1228481#post1228481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a simple mistake (especially for speakers of languages that handle articles differently).<br /> <br /> It's also a title that doesn't make perfect sense because the the story is largely from Louis' perspective, who is by far not &amp;quot;the&amp;quot; vampire, he's just &amp;quot;a&amp;quot; vampire. He's only &amp;quot;the&amp;quot; vampire to Daniel (who's not even named in Interview).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just being cheeky. I know why people get it wrong. It's the same people who saw the Berenstein Bears, think Nelson Mandela died in prison and believe it's 'Sex in the City' instead of 'Sex and the City'.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah and while we're at it: no, Darth Vader never actually said &quot;Luke, I'm your father&quot; and Sherlock Holmes also never said &quot;Elementary, my dear Watson&quot; yet people all over the world are convinced these are actual quotes of these characters.<br /> <br /> The Mandela effect is an interesting phenomenon for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":